    "self_validation_bound_fraction": 0.0029427129618654793
  },
  "warrant": "All x/y/z production components enter total vector power, magnitude, divergence and curl diagnostics. Density--div(Psi_1) anti-coherence and near-minus-one transfer test phase, sign, axis and k normalisation inside each realization, while curl/divergence ratios test longitudinal dominance for both LPT orders. These are stable under the legal RNG change and therefore carry tighter limits than realization-dependent band powers. Zeroing 2LPT, changing the power model, swapping/sign-flipping axes and breaking density--displacement alignment are targeted fault probes; the fixed-k production matter power independently distinguishes CLASS input physics."
